  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munderover><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>&#8734;</mo></munderover><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><munderover><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>&#8734;</mo></munderover><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><munderover><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>&#8734;</mo></munderover><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><munderover><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>&#8734;</mo></munderover><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><munderover><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>&#8734;</mo></munderover><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>We know the expansion of exponential functions as,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>+